d=0.0,span=This Regulation should also apply to Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies when acting as a provider or deployer of an AI system."],["This Regulation","Union institutions","bodies","offices","agencies","a provider","deployer","an AI system"],["",["23","NUM","","CARDINAL",["ROOT","23"]],"",["This","DET","this","",["det","Regulation"]],["Regulation","PROPN","","",["nsubj","apply"]],["should","AUX","","",["aux","apply"]],["also","ADV","","",["advmod","apply"]],["apply","VERB","","",["ROOT","apply"]],["to","ADP","","",["prep","apply"]],["Union","PROPN","","",["compound","institution"]],["institutions","NOUN","institution","",["pobj","to"]],"",["bodies","NOUN","body","",["conj","institution"]],"",["offices","NOUN","office","",["conj","body"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","office"]],["agencies","NOUN","agency","",["conj","office"]],["when","SCONJ","","",["advmod","act"]],["acting","VERB","act","",["advcl","apply"]],["as","ADP","","",["prep","act"]],["a","DET","","",["det","provider"]],"",["provider","NOUN","","",["pobj","as"]],["or","CCONJ","","",["cc","provider"]],["deployer","NOUN","","",["conj","provider"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","provider"]],["an","DET","","",["det","system"]],["AI","PROPN","","ORG",["compound","system"]],["system","NOUN","","",["pobj","of"]],""],"neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0"],[["neg=0.031,neu=0.919,pos=0.05,compound=0.1027,span=(24) If, and insofar as, AI systems are placed on the market, put into service, or used with or without modification of such systems for military, defence or national security purposes, those should be excluded from the scope of this Regulation regardless of which type of entity is carrying out those activities, such as whether it is a public or private entity.","neg=0.024,neu=0.883,pos=0.093,compound=0.539,span=As regards military and defence purposes, such exclusion is justified both by Article 4(2) TEU and by the specificities of the Member States’ and the common Union defence policy covered by Chapter 2 of Title V TEU that are subject to public international law, which is therefore the more appropriate legal framework for the regulation of AI systems in the context of the use of lethal force and other AI systems in the context of military and defence activities.","neg=0.037,neu=0.799,pos=0.165,compound=0.7717,span=As regards national security purposes, the exclusion is justified both by the fact that national security remains the sole responsibility of Member States in accordance with Article 4(2) TEU and by the specific nature and operational needs of national security activities and specific national rules applicable to those activities.","neg=0.0,neu=0.909,pos=0.091,compound=0.6369,span=Nonetheless, if an AI system developed, placed on the market, put into service or used for military, defence or national security purposes is used outside those temporarily or permanently for other purposes, for example, civilian or humanitarian purposes, law enforcement or public security purposes, such a system would fall within the scope of this Regulation.","neg=0.0,neu=0.859,pos=0.141,compound=0.6597,span=In that case, the entity using the AI system for other than military, defence or national security purposes should ensure the compliance of the AI system with this Regulation, unless the system is already compliant with this Regulation.","neg=0.077,neu=0.825,pos=0.098,compound=0.0865,span=AI systems placed on the market or put into service for an excluded purpose, namely military, defence or national security, and one or more non-excluded purposes, such as civilian purposes or law enforcement, fall within the scope of this Regulation and providers of those systems should ensure compliance with this Regulation.","neg=0.031,neu=0.87,pos=0.099,compound=0.4939,span=In those cases, the fact that an AI system may fall within the scope of this Regulation should not affect the possibility of entities carrying out national security, defence and military activities, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities, to use AI systems for national security, military and defence purposes, the use of which is excluded from the scope of this Regulation.","neg=0.0,neu=0.925,pos=0.075,compound=0.4215,span=An AI system placed on the market for civilian or law enforcement purposes which is used with or without modification for military, defence or national security purposes should not fall within the scope of this Regulation, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities."],["AI systems","the market","service","modification","such systems","military, defence or national security purposes","those","the scope","this Regulation","which type","entity","those activities","it","a public or private entity","military and defence purposes","such exclusion","Article","TEU","the specificities","the Member States","the common Union defence policy","Chapter","Title V TEU","that","public international law","which","the more appropriate legal framework","the regulation","AI systems","the context","the use","lethal force","other AI systems","the context","military and defence activities","national security purposes","the exclusion","the fact","national security","the sole responsibility","Member States","accordance","Article 4(2) TEU","the specific nature","operational needs","national security activities","specific national rules","those activities","an AI system","the market","service","military","defence","national security purposes","those","other purposes","example","civilian or humanitarian purposes","law enforcement","public security purposes","such a system","the scope","this Regulation","that case","the entity","the AI system","defence","national security purposes","the compliance","the AI system","this Regulation","the system","this Regulation","AI systems","the market","service","an excluded purpose","namely military","defence","national security","one or more non-excluded purposes","civilian purposes","law enforce