r, it is also important to establish that, in each of those exhaustively listed and narrowly defined situations, certain elements should be taken into account, in particular as regards the nature of the situation giving rise to the request and the consequences of the use for the rights and freedoms of all persons concerned and the safeguards and conditions provided for with the use.","neg=0.118,neu=0.857,pos=0.024,compound=-0.7964,span=In addition, the use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purpose of law enforcement should be deployed only to confirm the specifically targeted individual’s identity and should be limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time, as well as the geographic and personal scope, having regard in particular to the evidence or indications regarding the threats, the victims or perpetrator.","neg=0.0,neu=0.977,pos=0.023,compound=0.0772,span=The use of the real-time remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces should be authorised only if the relevant law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment and, unless provided otherwise in this Regulation, has registered the system in the database as set out in this Regulation.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=The reference database of persons should be appropriate for each use case in each of the situations mentioned above."],["order","those systems","a responsible and proportionate manner","it","each","those exhaustively listed and narrowly defined situations","certain elements","account","the nature","the situation","rise","the request","the consequences","the use","the rights","freedoms","all persons","the safeguards","conditions","the use","addition","the use","real-time’ remote biometric identification systems","publicly accessible spaces","the purpose","law enforcement","the specifically targeted individual’s identity","what","the period","time","the geo