,"DET","","",["det","system"]],["systems","NOUN","system","",["pobj","of"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","system"]],["the","DET","","",["det","difficulty"]],["resulting","VERB","result","",["amod","difficulty"]],["difficulty","NOUN","","",["conj","system"],[-1.4,""]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","difficulty"]],["challenging","VERB","challenge","",["pcomp","in"],[0.6,""]],["their","PRON","","",["poss","result"]],["results","NOUN","result","",["dobj","challenge"]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","challenge"]],["court","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"]],"",["in","ADP","","",["prep","by"]],["particular","ADJ","","",["amod","in"]],["by","ADP","","",["prep","difficulty"]],["natural","ADJ","","",["amod","person"],[1.5,""]],["persons","NOUN","person","",["pobj","by"]],["under","ADP","","",["prep","difficulty"]],["investigation","NOUN","","",["pobj","under"]],""],"neg=0.107,neu=0.789,pos=0.104,compound=-0.0639"],[["neg=0.053,neu=0.892,pos=0.055,compound=0.0276,span=(60) AI systems used in migration, asylum and border control management affect persons who are often in particularly vulnerable position and who are dependent on the outcome of the actions of the competent public authorities.","neg=0.023,neu=0.776,pos=0.2,compound=0.9013,span=The accuracy, non-discriminatory nature and transparency of the AI systems used in those contexts are therefore particularly important to guarantee respect for the fundamental rights of the affected persons, in particular their rights to free movement, non-discrimination, protection of private life and personal data, international protection and good administration.","neg=0.047,neu=0.876,pos=0.077,compound=0.6705,span=It is therefore appropriate to classify as high-risk, insofar as their use is permitted under relevant Union and national law, AI systems intended to be used by or on behalf of competent public authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies charged with tasks in the fields of migration, asylum and border control management as polygraphs and similar tools, for assessing certain risks posed by natural persons entering the territory of a Member State or applying for visa or asylum, for assisting competent public authorities for the examination, including related assessment of the reliability of evidence, of applications for asylum, visa and residence permits and associated complaints with regard to the objective to establish the eligibility of the natural persons applying for a status, for the purpose of detecting, recognising or identifying natural persons in the context of migration, asylum and border control management, with the exception of verification of travel documents.","neg=0.033,neu=0.967,pos=0.0,compound=-0.296,span=AI systems in the area of migration, asylum and border control management covered by this Regulation should comply with the relevant procedural requirements set by the Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council , the Directive 2013/32/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council , and other relevant Union law.","neg=0.03,neu=0.97,pos=0.0,compound=-0.296,span=The use of AI systems in migration, asylum and border control management should, in no circumstances, be used by Member States or Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies as a means to circumvent their international obligations under the UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees done at Geneva on 28 July 1951 as amended by the Protocol of 31 January 1967.","neg=0.052,neu=0.784,pos=0.163,compound=0.6249,span=Nor should they be used to in any way infringe on the principle of non-refoulement, or to deny safe and effective legal avenues into the territory of the Union, including the right to international protection."],["(60) AI systems","migration","asylum","border control management","persons","who","particularly vulnerable position","who","the outcome","the actions","the competent public authorities","The accuracy",", non-discriminatory nature","transparency","the AI systems","those contexts","respect","the fundamental rights","the affected persons","in particular their rights","free movement","-","discrimination","protection","private life","personal data","international protection","good administration","It","high-risk","their use","relevant Union","national law","AI systems","behalf","competent public authorities","Union institutions","bodies","offices","agencies","tasks","the fields","migration","asylum","border control management","polygraphs","similar tools","certain risks","natural persons","the territory","a Member State","visa","asylum","competent public authorities","the examination","related assessment","the reliability","evidence","applications","asylum","visa","residence permits","complaints","regard","the objective","the eligibility","the natural persons","a status","the purpose","natural persons","the context","migration","asylum","border control","management","the exception","verification","travel documents","AI systems","the area","migration","asylum","border control management","this Regulation","the relevant procedural requirements","the Regulation","(EC","the European Parliament","the Council","the Directive 2013/32/EU","the European Parliament","the Council","other relevant Union law","The use","AI systems","migration","asylum","border control management","no circumstances","Member States","Union institutions","bodies","offices","agencies","a means","their international obligations","the UN Convention","the Status","Refugees","Geneva","28 July","the Protocol","31 January","they","any way","the principle","safe and effective legal avenues","the territory","the Union","the right","international protection"],["",["60","NUM","","CARDINAL",["nummod","system"]],"",["AI","PROPN","","",["compound","system"]],["systems","NOUN","system","",["nsubj","affect"]],["used","VERB","use","",["acl","system"]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","use"]],["migration","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"]],"",["asylum","NOUN","","",["conj","migratio