igation to comply with the requirements of this Regulation, when the standardisation request has not been accepted by any of the European standardisation organisations, or when the relevant harmonised standards insufficiently address fundamental rights concerns, or when the harmonised standards do not comply with the request, or when there are delays in the adoption of an appropriate harmonised standard.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=Where such a delay in the adoption of a harmonised standard is due to the technical complexity of that standard, this should be considered by the Commission before contemplating the establishment of common specifications.","neg=0.0,neu=0.878,pos=0.122,compound=0.3612,span=When developing common specifications, the Commission is encouraged to cooperate with international partners and international standardisation bodies."],["121) Standardisation","a key role","technical solutions","providers","compliance","this Regulation","line","the state","the art","innovation","competitiveness","growth","the single market","Compliance","harmonised standards","Article","point","Regulation","EU","the European Parliament","the Council","which","the state","the art","a means","providers","conformity","the requirements","this Regulation","A balanced representation","interests","all relevant stakeholders","the development","standards","particular SMEs","consumer organisations","environmental and social stakeholders","accordance","Articles","Regulation","EU","No","order","compliance","the standardisation requests","the Commission","undue delay","the standardisation request","the Commission","the advisory forum","the Board","order","relevant expertise","the absence","relevant references","harmonised standards","the Commission","acts","consultation","the advisory forum","common specifications","certain requirements","this Regulation","The common specification","an exceptional fall back solution","the provider’s obligation","the requirements","th