,"",["dobj","put"]],["into","ADP","","",["prep","put"]],["service","NOUN","","",["pobj","into"]],["without","ADP","","",["prep","put"]],["the","DET","","",["det","authorisation"]],["authorisation","NOUN","","",["pobj","without"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","authorisation"]],["the","DET","","",["det","authority"]],["market","NOUN","","",["compound","surveillance"]],["surveillance","NOUN","","",["compound","authority"]],["authority","NOUN","","",["pobj","of"],[0.3,""]],"",["provided","VERB","provide","",["prep","put"]],["that","SCONJ","","",["mark","request"]],["such","ADJ","","",["amod","authorisation"]],["authorisation","NOUN","","",["nsubjpass","request"]],["is","AUX","be","",["auxpass","request"]],["requested","VERB","request","",["ccomp","provide"]],["during","ADP","","",["prep","request"]],["or","CCONJ","","",["cc","during"]],["after","ADP","","",["conj","during"]],["the","DET","","",["det","use"]],["use","NOUN","","",["pobj","after"]],["without","ADP","","",["prep","use"]],["undue","ADJ","","",["amod","delay"]],["delay","NOUN","","",["pobj","without"],[0.962,"without undue delay"]],""],"neg=0.012,neu=0.859,pos=0.129,compound=0.6308"],[["neg=0.046,neu=0.887,pos=0.066,compound=0.3641,span=(131) In order to facilitate the work of the Commission and the Member States in the AI field as well as to increase the transparency towards the public, providers of high-risk AI systems other than those related to products falling within the scope of relevant existing Union harmonisation legislation, as well as providers who consider that an AI system listed in the high-risk use cases in an annex to this Regulation is not high-risk on the basis of a derogation, should be required to register themselves and information about their AI system in an EU database, to be established and managed by the Commission.","neg=0.077,neu=0.923,pos=0.0,compound=-0.4939,span=Before using an AI system listed in the high-risk use cases in an annex to this Regulation, deployers of high-risk AI systems that are public authorities, agencies or bodies, should register themselves in such database and select the system that they envisage to use.","neg=0.0,neu=0.811,pos=0.189,compound=0.2732,span=Other deployers should be entitled to do so voluntarily.","neg=0.0,neu=0.82,pos=0.18,compound=0.6908,span=This section of the EU database should be publicly accessible, free of charge, the information should be easily navigable, understandable and machine-readable.","neg=0.081,neu=0.877,pos=0.041,compound=-0.2732,span=The EU database should also be user-friendly, for example by providing search functionalities, including through keywords, allowing the general public to find relevant information to be submitted upon the registration of high-risk AI systems and on the use case of high-risk AI systems, set out in an annex to this Regulation, to which the high-risk AI systems correspond.","neg=0.106,neu=0.804,pos=0.09,compound=-0.0772,span=Any substantial modification of high-risk AI systems should also be registered in the EU database.","neg=0.047,neu=0.835,pos=0.117,compound=0.4767,span=For high-risk AI systems in the area of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management, the registration obligations should be fulfilled in a secure non-public section of the EU database.","neg=0.054,neu=0.819,pos=0.127,compound=0.3818,span=Access to the secure non-public section should be strictly limited to the Commission as well as to market surveillance authorities with regard to their national section of that database.","neg=0.206,neu=0.794,pos=0.0,compound=-0.5267,span=High-risk AI systems in the area of critical infrastructure should only be registered at national level.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=The Commission should be the controller of the EU database, in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2018/1725.","neg=0.0,neu=0.933,pos=0.067,compound=0.3818,span=In order to ensure the full functionality of the EU database, when deployed, the procedure for setting the database should include the development of functional specifications by the Commission and an independent audit report.","neg=0.095,neu=0.905,pos=0.0,compound=-0.2732,span=The Commission should take into account cybersecurity risks when carrying out its tasks as data controller on the EU database.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=In order to maximise the availability and use of the EU database by the public, the EU database, including the information made available through it, should comply with requirements under the Directive (EU) 2019/882."],["order","the work","the Commission","the Member States","the AI field","the transparency","the public","providers","high-risk AI systems","those","products","the scope","relevant existing Union harmonisation legislation","providers","who","an AI system","the high-risk use cases","an annex","this Regulation","high-risk","the basis","a derogation","themselves","information","their AI system","an EU database","the Commission","an AI system","the high-risk use cases","an annex","this Regulation","deployers","high-risk AI systems","that","public authorities","agencies","bodies","themselves","such database","the system","that","they","Other deployers","This section","the EU database","charge","the information","The EU database","example","search functionalities","keywords","the general public","relevant information","the registration","high-risk AI systems","the use case","high-risk AI systems","an annex","this Regulation","which","Any substantial modification","high-risk AI systems","the EU database","high-risk AI systems","the area","law enforcement","migration","asylum","border control","management","the registration obligations","a secure non-public section","the EU database","Access","the secure non-public section","the Commission","to market","surveillance authorities","regard","their national section","that database","High-risk AI systems","the area","critical infrastructure","national level","The Commissio