ATE",["appos","Regulation"]],"",["Providers","NOUN","provider","",["nsubj","ensure"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","provider"]],["prospective","ADJ","","",["amod","provider"]],["providers","NOUN","provider","",["conj","provider"]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","provider"]],["the","DET","","",["det","sandbox"]],["AI","PROPN","","ORG",["nmod","sandbox"]],["regulatory","ADJ","","",["amod","sandbox"]],["sandbox","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"]],["should","AUX","","",["aux","ensure"]],["ensure","VERB","","",["ROOT","ensure"],[1.6,""]],["appropriate","ADJ","","",["amod","safeguard"]],["safeguards","NOUN","safeguard","",["dobj","ensure"],[1.4,""]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","ensure"]],["cooperate","VERB","","",["conj","ensure"]],["with","ADP","","",["prep","cooperate"]],["the","DET","","",["det","authority"]],["competent","ADJ","","",["amod","authority"],[1.3,""]],["authorities","NOUN","authority","",["pobj","with"]],"",["including","VERB","include","",["prep","cooperate"]],["by","ADP","","",["prep","include"]],["following","VERB","follow","",["pcomp","by"]],["their","PRON","","",["poss","guidance"]],["guidance","NOUN","","",["dobj","follow"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","follow"]],["acting","VERB","act","",["conj","follow"]],["expeditiously","ADV","","",["advmod","act"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","expeditiously"]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","act"]],["good","ADJ","","",["amod","faith"],[1.9,""]],["faith","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"],[1.8,""]],["to","PART","","",["aux","mitigate"]],["adequately","ADV","","",["advmod","mitigate"]],["mitigate","VERB","","",["advcl","cooperate"]],["any","DET","","",["det","risk"]],["identified","VERB","identify","",["amod","risk"]],["significant","ADJ","","",["amod","risk"],[0.8,""]],["risks","NOUN","risk","",["dobj","mitigate"],[-1.1,""]],["to","ADP","","",["prep","mitigate"]],["safety","NOUN","","",["pobj","to"],[1.8,""]],"",["health","NOUN","","",["conj","safety"]],"",["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","health"]],["fundamental","ADJ","","",["amod","right"]],["rights","NOUN","right","",["conj","health"]],["that","PRON","","",["nsubj","arise"]],["may","AUX","","",["aux","arise"]],["arise","VERB","","",["relcl","right"]],["during","ADP","","",["prep","arise"]],["the","DET","","",["det","development"]],["development","NOUN","","",["pobj","during"]],"",["testing","NOUN","","",["conj","development"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","testing"]],["experimentation","NOUN","","",["conj","testing"]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","development"]],["that","DET","","",["det","sandbox"]],["sandbox","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"]],""],"neg=0.007,neu=0.654,pos=0.089,compound=0.4654"],[["neg=0.029,neu=0.904,pos=0.067,compound=0.4019,span=(141) In order to accelerate the process of development and the placing on the market of the high-risk AI systems listed in an annex to this Regulation, it is important that providers or prospective providers of such systems may also benefit from a specific regime for testing those systems in real world conditions, without participating in an AI regulatory sandbox.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=However, in such cases, taking into account the possible consequences of such testing on individuals, it should be ensured that appropriate and sufficient guarantees and conditions are introduced by this Regulation for providers or prospective providers.","neg=0.0,neu=0.844,pos=0.156,compound=0.6597,span=Such guarantees should include, inter alia, requesting informed consent of natural persons to participate in testing in real world conditions, with the exception of law enforcement where the seeking of informed consent would prevent the AI system from being tested.","neg=0.0,neu=0.843,pos=0.157,compound=0.6707,span=Consent of subjects to participate in such testing under this Regulation is distinct from, and without prejudice to, consent of data subjects for the processing of their personal data under the relevant data protection law.","neg=0.048,neu=0.741,pos=0.211,compound=0.9517,span=It is also important to minimise the risks and enable oversight by competent authorities and therefore require prospective providers to have a real-world testing plan submitted to competent market surveillance authority, register the testing in dedicated sections in the EU database subject to some limited exceptions, set limitations on the period for which the testing can be done and require additional safeguards for persons belonging to certain vulnerable groups, as well as a written agreement defining the roles and responsibilities of prospective providers and deployers and effective oversight by competent personnel involved in the real world testing.","neg=0.035,neu=0.76,pos=0.205,compound=0.8957,span=Furthermore, it is appropriate to envisage additional safeguards to ensure that the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system can be effectively reversed and disregarded and that personal data is protected and is deleted when the subjects have withdrawn their consent to participate in the testing without prejudice to their rights as data subjects under the Union data protection law.","neg=0.0,neu=0.958,pos=0.042,compound=0.5859,span=As regards transfer of data, it is also appropriate to envisage that data collected and processed for the purpose of testing in real-world conditions should be transferred to third countries only where appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented, in particular in accordance with bases for transfer of personal data under Union law on data protection, while for non-personal data appropriate safeguards are put in place in accordance with Union law, such as Regulations (EU) 2022/868 (42) and (EU) 2023/2854 (43) of the European Parliament and of the Council."],["order","the process","development","the placing","the market","the high-risk AI systems","an annex","this Regulation","it","providers","prospective providers","such systems","a specific regime","those systems","real world conditions","an AI regulatory sandbox","such cases","account","the possible consequences","such testing","individuals","it","appropriate and sufficient guarantees","conditions","this Regulation","providers","prospective providers","Such guarantees","inter alia","informed consent","natural persons","testing","real world conditions","the exception","law enforcement","the seeking","informed consent","the AI system","Consent","subjects","such testing","this Regulation","prejudice","consent","data subjects","the processing","their personal data","the relevant data protection law","It","the risks","oversight","competent authorities","prospective providers","a real-world testing plan","competent market surveillance authority","the testing","dedicated sections","the EU database","subject","some limited exceptions","limitations","the period","which","the testing","additional safeguards","persons","certain vulnerable groups","a written agreement","the roles","responsibilities","prospective providers","deployers","effective oversight","competent personnel","the real world testing","it","additional safeguards","the predictions","recommendations","decisions","the AI system","personal data","the subjects","their consent","the testing","prejudice","their rights","data subjects","the Union data protection law","transfer","data","it","data","the purpose","testing","real-world conditions","third countries","appropriate and applicable safeguards","Union law","accordance","bases","transfer","personal data","Union law","data protection","non-personal data appropriate safeguards","place","accordance","Union law","Regulations","EU","EU","the European Parliament","the Council"],["",["141","NUM","","CARDINAL",["dep","be"]],"",["In","ADP","in","",["prep","be"]],["order","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"]],["to","PART","","",["aux","accelerate"]],["accelerate","VERB","","",["acl","order"]],["the","DET","","",["det","process"]],["process","NOUN","","",["dobj","accelerate"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","process"]],["development","NOUN","","",["pobj","of