 risks and ensuring an adequate level of cybersecurity protection, regardless of whether it is provided as a standalone model or embedded in an AI system or a product.To achieve those objectives, this Regulation should require providers to perform the necessary model evaluations, in particular prior to its first placing on the market, including conducting and documenting adversarial testing of models, also, as appropriate, through internal or independent external testing.In addition, providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risks should continuously assess and mitigate systemic risks, including for example by putting in place risk-management policies, such as accountability and governance processes, implementing post-market monitoring, taking appropriate measures along the entire model’s lifecycle and cooperating with relevant actors along the AI value chain.","idx":113,"match_words":["provider","general","purpose","model","present","systemic","risk","subject","addition","obligation","provide","provider","general","purpose","model","obligation","aim","identify","mitigate","risk","ensure","an adequate level","cybersecurity protection","regardless","provide","model","embed","an ai system","product","achieve","objective","this regulation","require","provider","perform","necessary","model","evaluation","particular","prior","its first placing","the market","include","conduct","document","adversarial testing","model","also","appropriate","internal or independent external testing","addition","provider","general","purpose","model","systemic","risk","assess","mitigate","systemic","risk","include","example","put","place","risk","management","policy","such","accountability","governance","process","implement","post","market","monitoring","take","appropriate","measure","entire","model","lifecycle","cooperate","relevant","actor","the ai value chain"],"words":["the","provider","of","general","purpose","ai","model","present","systemic","risk","should","be","subject","in